  THE SHAPE AXIS.  An overall error in the stellar M/L (or in the gas fraction) moves every amplitude
  together and cannot be calibrated away; the SEPARATION SLOPE is immune to it.  Forecast error on
  d log sigma / d log r_p for a sample of N pairs spread over 30-1000 kpc at the measured dispersions:
     N pairs    v_err = 40 km/s    v_err = 10 km/s
         500              0.056              0.047
        2000              0.028              0.024
       10000              0.012              0.011
       50000              0.006              0.005
  the framework's isolated branch and the cosmic-share point mass differ by 0.462 in slope, so a
  3-sigma separation on the SHAPE axis alone needs N = 65 pairs at this data quality.
  [PASS] D1 the framework's prediction and the cosmic-share prediction are distinguishable at all, and by how much   (amplitude axis: N = 384 pairs for 3 sigma at 40 km/s (122 at 10 km/s); shape axis: slopes differ by 0.46, N = 65 for 3 sigma.  Both are far below the 1900 pairs already in hand)

